WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.160
Speaker 1: The COVID pandemic in the United&nbsp;
States is becoming more and more politically red.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:12.640
A year ago, we wondered Would this happen?&nbsp;
And then six months ago we said this will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:17.120
probably happen. And then three months&nbsp;
ago we said the data is showing that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:22.640
is starting to actually happen. But now it's not&nbsp;
only completely undeniable the degree to which in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:31.200
the United States, COVID has become a Republican&nbsp;
killer, a Republican virus disproportionately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:39.120
is quite stunning and overwhelmingly the COVID&nbsp;
deaths are happening in counties that Donald Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:48.800
won and presumably, logically, overwhelmingly, it&nbsp;
is Trump voters who are dying from COVID at much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:55.760
higher rates than Biden voters now. Would it be&nbsp;
enough to influence an election at a congressional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:02.880
district level in a state federally? Really&nbsp;
still a question mark in terms of the math. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:08.640
as we've looked at with hypothetical numbers from&nbsp;
Florida a few months ago, if this continues to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:13.520
disproportionately a virus that kills Republicans&nbsp;
in the United States because Republicans are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:18.480
disproportionately unvaccinated, it actually&nbsp;
could come to make a difference. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:22.240
in something like the Florida gubernatorial&nbsp;
election, it's a bit of a stretch, but it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:27.360
possible. But let's look at the numbers that we&nbsp;
have now. First, the New York Times has a really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:34.160
good piece on this, which shows how the Partizan&nbsp;
gap has grown and grown and grown since January&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:40.560
1st, where it was only slightly more likely in&nbsp;
January that the COVID deaths were in the Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:45.760
counties rather than the Biden counties. Now&nbsp;
remember, this is a chart of COVID death rates.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:50.560
So for people saying, well, there's more people&nbsp;
or fewer people, no, no, no, this is the rate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:56.720
per 100000 people. In January, there was a&nbsp;
slightly higher rate of death in Trump voting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:04.560
counties than Biden counties. That gap has spread&nbsp;
and spread is starting around mid-September. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:10.080
has increased dramatically to the point where now,&nbsp;
as you can see here, the cumulative death rate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:18.400
is under 200 deaths per 100000 people in Biden&nbsp;
counties. And it is rapidly approaching 300 deaths&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:24.320
per 100000 people in Trump counties. That is a&nbsp;
huge, huge difference. Now there have been many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:31.680
attempts, I guess I would call them by various&nbsp;
right wingers of different stripes to explain this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:37.600
difference away by saying, Well, the difference&nbsp;
is whether in those places or. The difference is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:44.560
age in these places in Trump versus Biden&nbsp;
counties. But when you examine the data, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:51.280
not supported by fact. And as it's pointed out in&nbsp;
the New York Times article about these numbers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:57.520
if the difference was due to weather or age, we&nbsp;
would have seen that Partizan split last year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:04.160
but instead we are seeing a dramatic increase&nbsp;
in that Partizan split over the last few months.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:10.400
What we are seeing is a shift. In what determines&nbsp;
who is most likely to die, and I'll tell you what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:14.880
I mean by that at the start of the pandemic, we've&nbsp;
talked about this now, we've said this before.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:22.160
The deaths were most likely to be happening in the&nbsp;
places that had, we would call it the misfortune&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:28.320
of being early infection sites because of the&nbsp;
direct flights to and from the early infected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.440
regions of China and some countries in Europe,&nbsp;
like Italy. So you had New York, New York, New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:38.400
Jersey, you had Boston with that early conference&nbsp;
and many nonstop flights to Asia, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:43.920
and a few other spots that early that was what&nbsp;
indicated what who was getting hit the hardest.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:48.480
We now have a very different situation.&nbsp;
We now know about how the virus spreads.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:55.360
We now have it everywhere, so to speak. And&nbsp;
we now have vaccination widely available. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:01.840
now the biggest distinguishing factor between the&nbsp;
Trump counties and the Biden counties is the level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:10.000
of vaccination. Forty percent of Republican adults&nbsp;
are not vaccinated. Only 10 percent of Democratic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:17.040
registered adults are unvaccinated. That is why&nbsp;
the COVID deaths are concentrated not in major&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:22.320
metropolitan areas, but rather on a rate basis.&nbsp;
Remember, we're talking about a rate of death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:29.280
The deaths are increasingly concentrated, where&nbsp;
conservatives tend to live more suburban and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:36.640
rural areas because they have a far lower rate of&nbsp;
vaccination. Now, it doesn't just apply to deaths.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:44.720
If you look at cases, we are seeing a big Partizan&nbsp;
gap there as well. It was biggest in August&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:49.680
and now, thanks to the national decline in&nbsp;
COVID cases, although the last ten days make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:55.120
us wonder whether cases are going to go back&nbsp;
up, we now see still a Partizan gap on cases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.120 --> 00:05:01.520
but a slightly smaller one than we had in August.&nbsp;
So COVID is getting more and more politically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:07.920
red. It's not Republic. It's not a surprising&nbsp;
thing that we are seeing this increasingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:13.360
ravaged Republicans at this point in time. And&nbsp;
there is a good chance. I mean, even when we say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:19.760
look at the death rate in this Biden county,&nbsp;
it stands to reason that because Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:26.480
are disproportionately unvaccinated, that even&nbsp;
in Biden counties, the deaths happening there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:32.720
skew towards the Republican Party. So every&nbsp;
country is different in the United States.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:38.160
We increasingly are seeing this as a Republican&nbsp;
pandemic. Does it mean liberals can't die? Of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:46.480
course not. The virus doesn't discriminate on&nbsp;
the basis of politics. However, vaccination is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:52.960
the greatest indicator as to where we are&nbsp;
seeing the virus kill more versus fewer people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:58.480
and it is Republicans who are disproportionately&nbsp;
unvaccinated. So we're going to keep following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:03.280
these numbers. But it is a trend we expect it&nbsp;
is the trend we started to see and the degree to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:07.520
which we are now seeing it is quite stunning. Do&nbsp;
Republicans care even if they don't care about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:10.800
people that are dying? Maybe they don't. Maybe&nbsp;
they do. I don't know. You'd have to ask them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:16.560
at some point. Don't you think that they would&nbsp;
wake up and say, Hey, this is this is killing our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:21.840
voters more than it is killing their voters? And&nbsp;
merely from the perspective of like a pragmatic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:26.640
election strategy. At some point, you&nbsp;
would imagine they would start saying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:30.400
Hey, you know, I've been like, This isn't good.&nbsp;
Maybe we should go and get ourselves vaccinated.

